This might be more of a statistics question but I'll throw it out there just in case someone has any ideas... I'm using an unmarked ZIP model to predict values of abundance on hypothetical situations during which I hold all input parameters at their average values and only vary the parameter of interest (All continuous variables were standardized to 0 prior to analysis).  I have two categorical variables in my analysis though - both of which are involved in separate interactions.  Does anyone know how to hold these categorical values at their "average"?  Even if I put zero for all the parameters, the intercept still represents the reference variable....not really sure how to handle that - any advice would be appreciated!

